{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL85891W","title":"The Jewel of Seven Stars","authors":["Bram Stoker"],"firstPublished":1902,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #3781.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #3781","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3781"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1","title":"A Summons in the Night"},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2","title":"Strange Instructions"},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3","title":"The Watchers"},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4","title":"The Second Attempt"},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5","title":"More Strange Instructions"},{"id":"s6","label":"Ch. 6","title":"Suspicions"},{"id":"s7","label":"Ch. 7","title":"The Traveller’s Loss"},{"id":"s8","label":"Ch. 8","title":"The Finding of the Lamps"},{"id":"s9","label":"Ch. 9","title":"The Need of Knowledge"},{"id":"s10","label":"Ch. 10","title":"The Valley of the Sorcerer"},{"id":"s11","label":"Ch. 11","title":"A Queen’s Tomb"},{"id":"s12","label":"Ch. 12","title":"The Magic Coffer"},{"id":"s13","label":"Ch. 13","title":"Awaking From the Trance"},{"id":"s14","label":"Ch. 14","title":"The Birth-Mark"},{"id":"s15","label":"Ch. 15","title":"The Purpose of Queen Tera"},{"id":"s16","label":"Ch. 16","title":"The Cavern"},{"id":"s17","label":"Ch. 17","title":"Doubts and Fears"},{"id":"s18","label":"Ch. 18","title":"The Lesson of the “Ka”"},{"id":"s19","label":"Ch. 19","title":"The Great Experiment"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-trelawny","label":"Trelawny (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"margaret","name":"Margaret","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Once more, my dear Margaret, let me impress on you the need for observation and just reasoning to conclusions, howsoever strange.”"},{"id":"mr-trelawny","name":"Mr. Trelawny","role":"protagonist","group":"g-trelawny","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “We ascended to Mr.”"},{"id":"miss-trelawny","name":"Miss Trelawny","role":"protagonist","group":"g-trelawny","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““Miss Trelawny, sir, sent a man to tell us to get out a carriage at once; and when we was ready she come herself and gave me the letter and told Morgan—the coachman, sir—to fly.”"},{"id":"doctor-winchester","name":"Doctor Winchester","aliases":["Winchester"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Miss Trelawny introduced us: “Doctor Winchester, Mr.”"},{"id":"mr-corbeck","name":"Mr. Corbeck","aliases":["Corbeck"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: ““My name is Corbeck.”"},{"id":"silvio","name":"Silvio","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “That is my Silvio.”"},{"id":"queen","name":"Queen","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “Then they told me that a great Sorcerer in ancient days—‘millions of millions of years’ was the term they used—a King or a Queen, they could not say which, was buried there.”"},{"id":"sergeant-daw","name":"Sergeant Daw","aliases":["Daw"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “So I sent a note asking to have Sergeant Daw sent at once.”"},{"id":"mrs-grant","name":"Mrs. Grant","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““We lifted Father on a sofa; and the housekeeper, Mrs.”"},{"id":"queen-tera","name":"Queen Tera","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: ““Queen Tera was of the Eleventh, or Theban Dynasty of Egyptian Kings which held sway between the twenty-ninth and twenty-fifth centuries before Christ.”"},{"id":"mr-ross","name":"Mr. Ross","aliases":["Ross"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “You see, Mr.”"},{"id":"van-huyn","name":"Van Huyn","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “It was of little wonder that I had connected it with such a narrative; for if my eyes told me truly, here, in this room with me, was the very hand of which the traveller Van Huyn had written.”"},{"id":"malcolm-ross","name":"Malcolm Ross","aliases":["Malcolm"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: ““My name, as I told you, is Ross, Malcolm Ross.”"},{"id":"mr-marvin","name":"Mr. Marvin","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “My solicitors, Marvin & Jewkes, of 27B Lincoln’s Inn, have full instructions in case of my death; and Mr.”"},{"id":"superintendent","name":"Superintendent","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “So I said to the Superintendent:”"},{"id":"hathor","name":"Hathor","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “one on each, the seven forms of Hathor.”"},{"id":"kennedy","name":"Kennedy","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Nurse Kennedy, on the other hand, was rather under than over a woman’s average height.”"},{"id":"egyptians","name":"Egyptians","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “The Arabs were not bound by the same superstitious fears as the Egyptians; Sheik Abu Some and his following were willing to take a part in the explorations.”"},{"id":"sir-james-frere","name":"Sir James Frere","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: ““He is Sir James Frere.”"},{"id":"princess","name":"Princess","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: ““No wonder the house is like a King’s house, when the mistress is a Princess!””"},{"id":"sheik","name":"Sheik","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “I would fain have gone with my companions to seek him and give him sepulture of some kind; but the Sheik made light of it, and sent two of his men to see to it whilst we went on our way.”"},{"id":"chapel","name":"Chapel","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “Passing within the portico, we found two of the architectural features of a rock tomb, the Ch